course: dictionary
lesson: 7526
title: The wide, flat grasslands
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A prairie is a large, flat area of grassland with few trees. Context clues help you find this meaning. «The prairies of North America have very rich black soil, built from grass roots over thousands of years» tells you the land is covered in grass, not forest.
explain: Look for more clues. «Ukrainian farmers settling the Canadian Prairies» and «great farmlands for wheat» tell you the flat grassland is good for farming. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «farmers settling the large, flat grassland of Canada» still makes sense.
explain: Prairie can also be a name with a capital P. «The Prairies» means the grasslands of central USA and Canada, and the Prairie Provinces of Canada are Alberta, Saskatchewan and Manitoba.
fact: A prairie is a large, flat area of grassland with few trees.
fact: «The Prairies», with a capital P, is the name for the grasslands of central USA and Canada.
fact: Alberta, Saskatchewan and Manitoba are called the Prairie Provinces.
fact: Prairies are used for farming wheat and cattle, because their black soil is very rich.
fact: «Prairie dogs» are ground squirrels that live in huge underground towns with many entrances and rooms.
exercise: «The prairies of North America have very rich black soil, built from grass roots over thousands of years.» What is the prairie covered in? | Snow | *Grass | Water | Sand
exercise: In stories of the old West, «families travel across the prairie.» What kind of place is the prairie? | A busy city street | A snowy mountain top | The bottom of the sea | *A large, flat grassland
exercise: Which country has the Prairie Provinces of Alberta, Saskatchewan and Manitoba? | *Canada | Brazil | Japan | Australia
test: «Prairie dogs live in huge underground towns with many entrances and rooms.» What do their underground towns have? | Water pipes | A roof of glass | Only one door | *Many entrances and rooms
test: «Prairie dogs give alarm calls» when danger is near. Why do they give these calls? | To say goodbye | *To warn each other of a predator | To ask for food | To sing to the sun
exam: Mia says a prairie is a mountain range. Is she right? | Yes, it is a small lake | Yes, it is a deep, dark forest | Yes, it is a high, rocky mountain | *No, a prairie is a large, flat area of grassland
